statement: For one supplied true-column construction with standard forms/carriers, choose one B from its common level-zero positive space. For all words and all GIdx places the actual local lattices have frames j_v(B), with B* J0 B=I and every LI position identity retained. In canonical positive coordinates B=I works.
assumptions: ["The host CM field, real subfield, involution, ranks and true-column record are supplied exactly as in v0.12; this component does not prove their arithmetic existence.", "SF2/SF4/SF7 use the literal supplied Ok, Pins, Laws, Later and StdF/StdLvC/CarH/CarT premises. The complete colsTiedSym_std constructor remains an explicit unexpanded source input.", "LI1--LI7 supply the local completion, splitting, prime bijection, iw embedding and original coefficient/complex position alignment. Their choices are retained.", "The Hermitian dual uses E-valued integrality with conjugation in the first argument. It is not a trace dual.", "A common B is asserted for one fixed global construction. There is no assertion of a single B across different arithmetic hosts or unrelated parameter choices.", "This component proves neither class-rank equality nor the comparison-map representation identity or global integral span; other components must provide those arguments.", "The complete colsTiedSym_std constructor, host/point existence and remaining compatibility fields remain explicit source inputs. This theorem supplies StdB/fr_B and the companion algebra, not the full CmpTied representation identity."]
